{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1325145-quick-question-about-spirits","id":1325145,"title":"Quick Question About Spirits.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-07-16T21:02:16-07:00","id":1325145,"title":"Quick Question About Spirits.","content":"Hi everyone,I'm a long time Forsaken fan,and I thought I'd take a look at Apocalypse,great game. I have a important question though,how varied are spirits in Apocalypse? In Forsaken ,everything has a spirit. Places,emotions,abstract concepts,anything really. Is it the same on Apocalypse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T23:28:40-07:00","id":1325165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1325145-quick-question-about-spirits#post1325145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi everyone,I'm a long time Forsaken fan,and I thought I'd take a look at Apocalypse,great game. I have a important question though,how varied are spirits in Apocalypse? In Forsaken ,everything has a spirit. Places,emotions,abstract concepts,anything really. Is it the same on Apocalypse?</div> </div> </div> </div>Its the same in Apocalypse animistic so emotions have spirits and specific things like trees have Spirits. In a region every animal won't have a spirit but if there are populations of animals there will start being one or more spirit popping up to represent them. So a new city with no cats won't have cat spirits, but say you start having strays wonder in a Cat spirit representing the strays will pop up, and if their populations increases there could be more cat spirits popping up.<br /> <br /> The biggest difference is in Foresaken the Spirits are all predatory and self interested, and often neutral at best. In Apocalypse, there are a lot more neutral spirits and there are even salubrious spirits that can exist peacefully and harmoniously. In Foresaken even peace or joy spirits can become predatory and force their emotions to the detriment of mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T23:31:05-07:00","id":1325166,"title":"","content":"Thank you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni